  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1055 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nWe won't see much change in the weather pattern on Friday and\nSaturday with short waves continuing to spin around the upper\nlevel ridge. This will keep a medium chance for scattered showers\nand thunderstorms in the forecast with the highest chances\nduring the afternoon and evenings. We will see plenty of CAPE but\nlapse rates and shear stay poor keeping the severe threat low.\nPWATs will tick up some and heavy rain will be likely with any\nthunderstorms. On Saturday a trough pushing into the Great Lakes\nwill flatten the ridge some and pushing the better forcing to our\nsouth. We will still hold onto a low chance for scattered showers\nand thunderstorms. Zonal flow to weak troughing sets up next week\nbringing low to medium chances for showers and thunderstorms. \nHighs will remain in the low to mid 90s with afternoon heat index \nvalues near 100.",
